    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a26">

                <pb facs="0494" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg484"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 29 in No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Gunnison to the Mayor
                        of Halifax.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 19, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> As it is evident, from what has just
                    transpired on the Queen’s wharf, that the pirates of the Chesapeake cannot be
                    arrested in this city, I therefore feel it incumbent on me to notify you that
                    the United States government at present will not require the further services of
                    the police of this city.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>NATHANIEL GUNNISON, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Vice-Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
